cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Space Radar in your work or teaching, please cite it as below. The data it draws belongs to its publishers: see CREDITS.md."
title: "Space Radar: a live 3D map of space in the browser"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Space Radar contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sara-Managed-Projects/space-radar"
url: "https://www.spaceradar.ai"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Space Radar is a free, open-source, static website that draws the satellites around the Earth, the planets and
  their moons, the stars, nebulae and narrated trips at their real positions, computed in the visitor's browser
  from public data. Every drawn thing is labelled as measured, modelled or illustrative, and every fact names its
  source. It needs no account and no build step, and it runs offline from a downloaded copy.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - satellite tracking
  - planetarium
  - exoplanets
  - education
  - open data
  - three.js
